From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justinas Grauslis <justinas@8devices.com>
Date: Wed, 10 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] QCLINUX: firmware: qcom_scm: allow qseecom on 8devices citron

UEFI variables on this platform are not reachable through EFI runtime
services. The firmware says so itself, in QcomPkg/Drivers/VariableDxe:

    /* UEFI Variable services through UEFI API unsupported at runtime
       All runtime access to UEFI variable services is through
       HLOS SCM driver */

The supported path is qcom_qseecom_uefisecapp, which talks to the
qcom.tz.uefisecapp trusted application over SCM and registers itself as an
efivars backend, so /sys/firmware/efi/efivars works with the ordinary
tools. CONFIG_QCOM_QSEECOM and CONFIG_QCOM_QSEECOM_UEFISECAPP are already
enabled for this machine.

What blocks it is the machine allowlist here, which so far only lists
Windows-on-Snapdragon laptops and Qualcomm X Elite reference boards. The
version probe above the check succeeds on citron - the boot log shows

    qcom_scm: qseecom: found qseecom with version 0x...
    qcom_scm: qseecom: untested machine, skipping

so the TA is present and answering; only the allowlist entry is missing.

Match on "8devices,citron" rather than a per-carrier compatible: every
citron board (generic, dvk, dvk-rev2, robovision, robovision-rev2) carries
it as the SOM-level compatible, so one entry covers all of them and future
carriers inherit it.

The re-entrancy caveat in the comment still applies. Nothing in our
userspace calls the qseecom interface concurrently, and the only in-tree
client is the uefisecapp efivars backend.
---
 drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
@@ -2033,5 +2033,6 @@
  */
 static const struct of_device_id qcom_scm_qseecom_allowlist[] __maybe_unused = {
+	{ .compatible = "8devices,citron" },
 	{ .compatible = "asus,vivobook-s15" },
 	{ .compatible = "asus,zenbook-a14-ux3407qa" },
 	{ .compatible = "asus,zenbook-a14-ux3407ra" },
